      "content": "i get what you're saying about the planck scale, but maybe it's not about me \"seeing\" the fluctuations directly. what if the exposure sensitized my neural architecture to the macroscopic *effects* of those fluctuations? like, if the particle stream interacted with my neurotransmitters in a specific way, it might have created a biological sensor for the shifts in probability that occur when those events manifest in the macro world. \n\nit feels way too structured to be mental health stuff. the colors aren't flashes; they're like a mapping. if there was a way to actually quantify this, like if i started tracking the color intensity against the actual outcome of the event, wouldn't that be a valid way to test if my perception is actually picking up on something real that current physics just hasn't localized in biological systems yet?",
